<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco de Ibarra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1539–<a href="/years/1575">1575</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibarra">Ibarra</a> was a Basque explorer funded by his uncle Diego de Ibarra, one of the founders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zacatecas">Zacatecas</a>. From 1554 he led expeditions north, founded Durango in 1563 and became the first governor of the province of Nueva <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Vizcaya</a>. He explored as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonora">Sonora</a> region and opened new silver mines in the north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-de-ibarra.jpg" alt="Francisco de Ibarra" width="230" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francisco_de_Ibarra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
